Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Web: expose the Wasm worker's script URL

A Web Assembly worker runs from a blob URL that holds Squadron's loader
script, so inside the worker self.location is the blob, not the worker's
files. Code in the worker that loads sibling assets (a wasm-bindgen
module next to the worker, for instance) has no reliable base URL and
ends up guessing from the origin.

The loader already derives the absolute URL of the worker's .wasm file.
Assign it to globalThis.squadronWorkerScriptUrl right after deriving it,
before the Dart runtime is imported or main is invoked, so the worker
can resolve relative paths against its real location. self.location,
the blob, the worker packaging and the channel protocol are unchanged.
JavaScript workers do not need it: they run from their own URL.
---
 CHANGELOG.md                            | 1 +
 lib/src/_impl/web/_entry_point_uri.dart | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 939b738..7726369 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 - Add `Worker.channelFactory` (and a `channelFactory` constructor parameter) so a worker can open its channel somewhere other than an isolate or a Web Worker, e.g. another process over a socket. Without a factory, `Worker.start()` opens `Channel.open()` as before.
 - Export `SquadronCancelationToken` and `StreamId`, which custom `Channel` implementations need.
+- Web: the loader of a Web Assembly worker sets `globalThis.squadronWorkerScriptUrl` to the absolute URL of the worker's `.wasm` file before it loads the Dart runtime. The worker runs from a blob URL, so `self.location` cannot tell it where its own files are.
 
